<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformation Eliminated
  =====================================================
  This Web.Release.config transformation file has been deprecated and is no longer
  applied during builds. All environment-specific configuration (including
  connection strings, compilation debug flags, and feature flags) is now
  externalized to runtime environment variables and AWS Systems Manager (SSM)
  Parameter Store.

  MIGRATION SUMMARY
  -----------------
  Previously this file used XDT transforms (e.g., RemoveAttributes(debug)) to
  strip debug settings and inject release-specific values at build time, creating
  environment-baked artifacts that could not be promoted across environments
  without rebuilding.

  The application now reads configuration at runtime using the following
  priority order (see DAL/myDAL.cs CreateConnection()):

    1. RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING  - Full SQL Server connection string
                                      (retrieved from AWS SSM Parameter Store
                                       and injected as an environment variable
                                       by ECS task definition / Elastic Beanstalk)

    2. Individual RDS Proxy variables (assembled into a connection string):
         RDS_PROXY_ENDPOINT  - RDS Proxy endpoint hostname
         RDS_DB_NAME         - Target database name
         RDS_DB_USER         - Database user name
         RDS_DB_PASSWORD     - Database password (or IAM authentication token)
         RDS_DB_PORT         - Port (optional, defaults to 1433)

    3. DB_CONNECTION_STRING - Fallback for local development only

  AWS SSM PARAMETER STORE INTEGRATION
  ------------------------------------
  Store environment-specific parameters under a path hierarchy, e.g.:
    /clinic-mgmt/staging/RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING
    /clinic-mgmt/prod/RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING

  Inject them into the running container/instance via:
    - ECS Task Definition: "secrets" or "environment" sections
    - Elastic Beanstalk: Environment Properties or .ebextensions
    - AWS AppConfig: for dynamic, hot-reloadable configuration

  COMPILATION DEBUG FLAG
  ----------------------
  The <compilation debug="true"> attribute previously removed by this transform
  is now controlled by the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT / DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT variable:
    - Development  -> debug behaviour enabled
    - Production   -> debug behaviour disabled (default for cloud deployments)

  This approach enables immutable build artifacts that are promoted unchanged
  from development through staging to production, satisfying 12-factor app
  principle III (Config).
-->

<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No XDT transforms are applied. Configuration is injected at runtime via
    environment variables and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.
    See the comment block above for details.
  -->
</configuration>
